# Per-installation configuration. Copy to board.env (gitignored) and fill in.
# Nothing here is secret: secrets live in `pass` and in the Kubernetes secret. This file
# holds the values that differ between installations — hostnames, the owner's name, the
# cluster context.

# --- the board service ------------------------------------------------------
# Public hostname of the board. Used for the ingress and for the links the board puts in
# push notifications.
BOARD_HOST=board.example.com

# The owner's name on the board: the actor string that appears in events, `answered_by`,
# `pinned_by` and on the HTML pages. Keep it STABLE for the life of a board — changing it
# means the history rows stop matching the new identity, and the human gate no longer
# recognizes old answers as human answers.
BOARD_HUMAN=human

# Where the board pushes notifications. An ntfy topic URL, or empty to disable pushes
# entirely (the board then never notifies; the /status and /tests pages still work).
NTFY_URL=

# kubectl context for k8s/deploy.sh. Empty means the current context.
KUBE_CONTEXT=

# --- agent-side (exported in the shell that runs /next) ---------------------
# Where the CLI reaches the board. Agents export this; it defaults to localhost:8080.
#   export BOARD_URL=https://board.example.com
#
# Tokens are NOT set here. bin/board fetches them from `pass`:
#   pass board/token          the agent token, on every call
#   pass board/human-token    the human token, only in a shell with no agent harness
# See README.md, "Security".
